 5.34, "poll_margin": 22.92, "poll_sd": 5.32, "poll_weight": 0.5, "fundamentals": {"margin": 7.35, "lean": -0.75, "environment": 4.1, "incumbency": 4.0, "money": 0.0}, "rating_margin": 16.0, "sigma_race": 6.0, "sigma_total": 6.4, "baseline_margin": 17.75, "analyst_adjustment": 1.75, "key_factors": ["Every public poll since June shows Shapiro ahead by 19 to 27 points, including surveys from Republican-affiliated firms", "All seven expert raters place the race in the Solid or Safe Democratic column", "Prediction markets price Shapiro's re-election at 97-98 percent", "Garrity has campaigned actively and debated but has not closed the gap in any survey"], "rationale": "Polls from across the methodological and partisan spectrum show Shapiro leading by roughly 20 points, raters unanimously call the race Solid or Safe Democratic, and markets price his win near certainty. The state's slight Republican lean and normal limits on incumbents' margins temper the number somewhat below the raw polling average, but he remains a heavy favorite.", "watch": "A major late-breaking scandal or a sharp national shift toward Republicans could narrow the race, though current polling and markets show no sign of tightening.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Josh Shapiro (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Governor Josh Shapiro seeks a second term against Republican State Treasurer Stacy Garrity, with Libertarian Ken Krawchuk also on the ballot. Every recent public poll shows Shapiro ahead by double digits, with margins of roughly 19 to 27 points across surveyors of differing partisan affiliations. Aggregated polling places his lead near 23 points as of early October.\n\nAll seven major race raters place the contest in the Solid or Safe Democratic column, and prediction markets put Shapiro's odds at 97 to 98 percent. Garrity has campaigned on taxes and immigration, including a scheduled debate, but no public survey shows the race narrowing. Shapiro's national profile, highlighted by a 